+# Synthetic fixture format
+
+`cases.json` is deterministically regenerated by `scripts/compare.cjs`.
+`w`/`h` are quality-field dimensions, `md` is saturation distance, `fill` is initial wetness; `rects` are [x0,y0,x1,y1,wet] overrides with half-open bounds. Alternatively `mask` is a full row-major 0/1 array. `edits` are ordered [linearIndex, finalWet] entries, with last write winning. `quality` identifies actual production field dimensions where present, not a captured real room. Bridge and logical-tile fixtures are labelled synthetic. `.rgba` outputs are complete fields, not patches.
